<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/70218%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Aqueduct? supplying Augustodurum";
    rdfs:comment "In the 19th century, A. de Caumont hypothesized an aqueduct to supply Augustodurum from the south (i.e., from the modern communes of Juaye-Mondaye and Monceaux-en-Bessin). This idea was repeated in TIR Condate whence BAtlas, but more recently it has been called into question.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/70218> .

