<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/705365883%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Başkale";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/214160492%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "Başkale (Turkish \"Main Castle\") is a town and district located in Van Province in south-eastern Turkey. According to an inscription in the Urartean language of the Urartean king Minua (9th/8th century BCE) on a stone block (A 5-52), the fortress located here was built by Minua. It was given the name \"City of the God Haldi\".";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/705365883> .

