    rdfs:label "Santa Sabina";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/423025%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "A Christian basilica on the Aventine Hill in Rome was founded in the fourth century A.D. The church takes its name from a Christian martyr who was said to have lived on the Aventine. The church is the oldest extant Roman basilica structure that preserves its original plan in the city of Rome.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/715215852> .

