<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/716656%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Zygris (Marsa Baqqush)";
    rdfs:comment "An ancient anchorage on the Mediterranean coast of modern Egypt mentioned by Ptolemy (Zygis limen) and in the Stadiasmus Maris Magni. This Zygris (not to be confused with another also mentioned by Ptolemy) has been identified since the early 20th century with a small, reef-walled bay whose name, Marsa Baqqush, has since come to denote the larger bay of which the Zygris anchorage is a part. Multiple ancient wrecks have been identified within and just outside this anchorage, and an extensive system of interconnected rock-cut cisterns, elliptically mentioned in the Stadiasmus, has been identified ashore.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/716656> .

<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/716656/imagery-location-of-marsa-baqqush> dcterms:creator <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/thomase>;
    dcterms:description "Location verified in Google Earth with reference to coordinates and figures in Khalil 2024.";
    dcterms:modified "2025-09-24T19:35:07-04:00";
