<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/71706222%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Temple F at Selinus";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/462489%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "Temple F at Selinus is a Doric temple located on the site's so-called \"East Hill\". Dedicated either to Athena or Dionysus, the temple dates to the middle of the sixth century B.C. The non-canonical ground plan of 6 x 14 columns gives the temple an elongated aspect.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/71706222> .

