<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/719936358%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Adad Gate";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/874621%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/882947620%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/945930916%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "The northern city wall of Nineveh had three gates: the Adad Gate was the easternmost of the three. The Neo-Assyrian king Sennacherib constructed it and gave it the Akkadian ceremonial name Adad-šārik-hegalli-ana-māti, which means \"The God Adad Is the Provider of Prosperity to the Land.\"";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/719936358> .

