    rdfs:label "Veliki Preslav";
    rdfs:comment "Veliki Preslav was a fortified site that served as the capital of the Tsar Simeon I of the Bulgarian Empire. The site flourished during the ninth and tenth centuries CE. The site includes both 'inner' and 'outer' fortified areas.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/731893155> .

