<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/732224173%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "tomb of C. Sulpicius Platorinus";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/423025%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "A monumental family tomb dating to the late Augustan period was discovered in 1880 on the embankments of the Tiber River. This tomb was situated in the transtiberim at the head of the Pons Agrippae. It is associated with the gens of the Sulpicii Platorini. The tomb was reconstructed in 1911 at the Museo Nazionale Romano in 1911.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/732224173> .

<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/732333582%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Monumenti Funerari Romani";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/432617%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "An archaeological area at Avella includes a sector of the ancient monumental necropolis that was in use between the late Hellenistic period and the early imperial period. It lies along an extra-urban road axis. Remains of four Roman mausolea are presently visible.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/732333582> .

