<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/742516213%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Hagi/Aği/Kocapınar";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/801408827%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "Kocapınar (known as Hagi/Aği until officially renamed in 1959) is a modern town in the administrative district of Erciş in the Van Province in eastern Turkey. Here a stela with an inscription of Argišti II., son of Rusa (8th / 7th century BCE) was found which reports the creation of an artificial lake in front of Mount Quria.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/742516213> .

