<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/745915669%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Velletri-Stimmate";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/423117%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "At Velletri the remains of a Late Archaic sanctuary (ca. 530 BCE) were discovered beneath the church of the SS. Stimmate di S. Francesco. The site is often referred to as \"Tempio delle Stimmate\"; Cardinal Stefano Borgia discovered it in 1784. The architectural terracottas from the sanctuary are part of the so-called \"Veio-Roma-Velletri\" decorative system.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/745915669> .

