<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/747002130%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Building IV on the Athenian Acropolis";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/638356144%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/993507722%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "A building at the southeast end of the Acropolis of Athens, built perhaps in the 440s BC. Suggested identifications include the workshop for construction of the Parthenon, the hero shrine of Pandion (the eponymous hero of the tribe Pandionis), and the Chalkotheke. It is now covered by the Old Acropolis Museum.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/747002130> .

