<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/748147226%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Khorsabad Palace F";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/175106248%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/21271257%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/4517388%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/460169767%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/874458%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "The armory (ekal māšarti) of Dūr-Šarrukīn (modern Khorsabad) was located in the lower city, adjacent to the southern stretch of the southwest wall. No inscriptions of the eighth-century-BC Assyrian king Sargon II (r. 721–705 BC) record the construction of \"Palace F,\" although several objects of that ruler were discovered there.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/748147226> .

