<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/749106645%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Tiszapolgár-Basatanya";
    rdfs:comment "A Chalcolithic cemetery located at modern Polgár, Hungary, with at least 156 graves. This site is the typesite for the Tiszapolgár or Tiszapolgár-Româneşti culture, an Eneolithic archaeological culture. This archaeological culture has been identified on the Great Hungarian Plain and elsewhere in eastern, central Europe. It dates ca. 4500-4000 BCE.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/749106645> .

