<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/7591735%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Avatha";
    rdfs:comment "Avatha (al-Bakhra') is the site of a Late Roman and early Islamic fort that is located south of Palmyra. The fort was originally a Tetrarchic establishment that housed an auxiliary cavalry unit. The fort was modified and expanded during the Umayyad period.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/7591735> .

