    rdfs:comment "The Stoa of Attalos, located on the eastern side of the ancient Athenian agora, is a long, rectangular, two-story building of limestone and marble, with an external and internal colonnade. It was originally constructed around 150 BCE and then reconstructed in the 1950s.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/759679649> .

