<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/768485974%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Segouiola";
    rdfs:comment "Segouiola was an old Spanish village located in the west of the province of Sevilla during the kingdom of Alfonso X. Previously, the Arab population called it Boriauenzohar. Afterwards, this place assumed other names, including Torre del Guadiamar. Since the nineteenth century, Torre del Guadiamar county has been part of Benacazón.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/768485974> .

