<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/769421955%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Castle of Oria";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/541131%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "The Castle of Oria is a fortification complex on the northern side of Tempe valley of Peneus river, between Mount Olympus and Mount Ossa, in Thessaly, Greece. It played a critical role in defending the region during the Byzantine period. Evidence for the fortifications’ existence in the area can be traced back to a now lost inscription dated to 48 BC. The tower of Oria has traces from several construction periods during the Byzantine period.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/769421955> .

