<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/774612717%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "South Etruria Survey area";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/222169303%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/413062%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/413121%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/413224%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/413328%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/413381%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/422868%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/422928%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/423076%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/423116%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/532728731%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/858395099%23this>,
        <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/963165127%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "The original and pioneering South Etruria Survey was led by J.B. Ward-Perkins of the British School at Rome from the 1950s to the 1970s. The initial focus was the territory of the city of Veii (Ager Veientanus). A revisiting of this survey area and the project's outcomes was part of the Tiber Valley Project led by Helen Patterson and initiated in 1997.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/774612717> .

