<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/786014015%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Abu Ballas";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/466778575%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "A sandstone peak approximately 200 kilometers southwest of the Dakhleh Oasis, containing extensive pottery remains dated from the 3rd millennium BCE through the Roman period. Abu Ballas was likely a way station along a caravan route connecting the Dakhleh Oasis with Gilf Kebir.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/786014015> .

