<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/78619237%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Asomata";
    rdfs:comment "Burial site located southeast of Mount Vermion. The site was primarily used during the Archaic period (mid 6th-early 5th centuries BCE), with additional burials through the late Classical-early Hellenistic period and some additional signs of earlier human activity from the Middle Neolithic period through the Bronze Age. Rescue excavations were conducted on the site in 2000-2002 during the construction of the Egnatia Highway.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/78619237> .

<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/78619237/google-earth-location-of-asomata-site> dcterms:creator <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/gmckee>;
