    rdfs:label "Alchester";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/973264595%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "Alchester was the site of a fortified Roman town located 17 kilometers to the northeast of Oxford. The site was of Claudian date and likely on the site of a Pre-Roman Iron Age settlement. It may have been one of the earliest legionary bases in Britannia.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/79289> .

