<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/79396%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Colerne";
    rdfs:comment "The remains of a Romano-British villa with at least 12 rooms were first uncovered via ploughing in 1838 on a tract of land called \"The Allotment\" near Colerne, Wiltshire, England. Excavations took place in 1854. Fragments of an inscribed mosaic reading either \"Servivs\" or \"Severvs\" were documented at the site.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/79396> .

