<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/794311060%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Assur Archive 21";
    spatial:C <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/893945%23this>;
    rdfs:comment "In what seems to be a Neo-Assyrian layer inside a Parthian house in hC10IV, excavators found the remains of a library, consisting of about 20 fragmentary clay tablets. The largest group of texts are incantations, but the library also included a prayer, lexical lists and a list of persons, as well as a literary text detailing the netherworld vision of an Assyrian prince. One of the texts, a memorandum, dates to the reign of Sin-šarru-iškun (ca. 626–612 BC).";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/794311060> .

<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/794311060/assur-archive-21> dcterms:creator <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/tseidler>;
