<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/79621%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Norton Disney";
    rdfs:comment "A Romano-British villa was identified at Norton Disney in 1933. This villa site has its origins in the first century CE and continued in use until the mid-fourth century. There were several architectural phases, the most elaborate of which included a corridor-type villa, a bath complex, a basilica-type hall, and a system of perimeter defenses.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/79621> .

