    rdfs:label "Sorviodunum";
    rdfs:comment "Sorviodunum (Old Sarum) is the site of pre-Roman habitation in Salisbury, England, where occupation began as early as 3,000 B.C. The oval Pre-Roman fort, covering some 11 ha, was re-used during the Roman and Norman periods.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/79688> .

