<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/79720%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Totternhoe Roman Villa";
    rdfs:comment "This Roman courtyard villa that yielded ceramics dating to the 4th century CE was located on what is now Church Farm in Totternhoe (Central Bedfordshire, England). The survey and excavations were published in the 1950s; the site was backfilled after excavation and the villa's remains are no longer visible.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/79720> .

