<https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/79726%23this> a <http://geovocab.org/spatial#Feature>;
    rdfs:label "Uley";
    rdfs:comment "At West Hill, Uley, Gloucestershire, excavations revealed the remains of a multi-period ritual site. This site remained in use from the Neolithic period to the Middle Ages. An Iron Age sanctuary was replaced by a Romano-British temple dedicated to Mercury in the early second century A.D.";
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/79726> .

