    dcterms:description "Başkale (Turkish \"Main Castle\") is a town and district located in Van Province in south-eastern Turkey. According to an inscription in the Urartean language of the Urartean king Minua (9th/8th century BCE) on a stone block (A 5-52), the fortress located here was built by Minua. It was given the name \"City of the God Haldi\".";
