    dcterms:creator <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/jbecker>;
    dcterms:description "At Velletri the remains of a Late Archaic sanctuary (ca. 530 BCE) were discovered beneath the church of the SS. Stimmate di S. Francesco. The site is often referred to as \"Tempio delle Stimmate\"; Cardinal Stefano Borgia discovered it in 1784. The architectural terracottas from the sanctuary are part of the so-called \"Veio-Roma-Velletri\" decorative system.";
