    dcterms:contributor <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/jbecker>;
    dcterms:creator <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/zrosalinsky>;
    dcterms:description "A Chalcolithic cemetery located at modern Polgár, Hungary, with at least 156 graves. This site is the typesite for the Tiszapolgár or Tiszapolgár-Româneşti culture, an Eneolithic archaeological culture. This archaeological culture has been identified on the Great Hungarian Plain and elsewhere in eastern, central Europe. It dates ca. 4500-4000 BCE.";
