    dcterms:coverage "Colerne";
    dcterms:creator <http://viaf.org/viaf/92609475>;
    dcterms:description "The remains of a Romano-British villa with at least 12 rooms were first uncovered via ploughing in 1838 on a tract of land called \"The Allotment\" near Colerne, Wiltshire, England. Excavations took place in 1854. Fragments of an inscribed mosaic reading either \"Servivs\" or \"Severvs\" were documented at the site.";
