    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "",
        "GeoNames 10346314: Tomb of the Shields and Chairs",
        "Wikidata Q101529172: Tomb of the Shields and Chairs, Caere";
    dcterms:creator <https://pleiades.stoa.org/author/jbecker>;
    dcterms:description "The so-called Tomb of the Shields and Chairs at Caere dates ca. 520 - 500 B.C. The organization of this tomb is similar to that of the Tomb of the Capitals and the Tomb of the Cornice. It has a short dromos and a large vestibule. In the vestibule are two seats carved from the tuff bedrock as well as a series of hanging shields carved in relief.";
